Subject: run-command: no pthread_setcancelstate() on bionic

Why: atfork_prepare()/atfork_parent() disable thread cancellation around fork() with
pthread_setcancelstate(). bionic implements no thread cancellation and has neither the function
nor PTHREAD_CANCEL_DISABLE, so run-command.c does not compile. Without cancellation there is
nothing to disable: a no-op that reports success.
Source: written for this module (see ndk/REFERENCES.md). termux-packages
packages/git/run-command.c.patch (commit b3baca4292b14c2dcded94058b2cc272dcb32b32) removes the two
calls under __ANDROID__ instead.

--- a/run-command.c
+++ b/run-command.c
@@ -18,6 +18,18 @@
 #include "packfile.h"
 #include "compat/nonblock.h"

+#if defined(__BIONIC__) && !defined(PTHREAD_CANCEL_DISABLE)
+/* bionic has no thread cancellation: nothing to disable around fork() */
+#define PTHREAD_CANCEL_DISABLE 0
+static inline int bionic_setcancelstate(int state UNUSED, int *oldstate)
+{
+	if (oldstate)
+		*oldstate = 0;
+	return 0;
+}
+#define pthread_setcancelstate bionic_setcancelstate
+#endif
+
 void child_process_init(struct child_process *child)
 {
 	struct child_process blank = CHILD_PROCESS_INIT;
